Build utls certificate decompression against brotli 1.2.7 and klauspost/compress 1.20.2

FORK DEVIATION: not upstream code. The utls this pin requires, aa6edf4b11af, takes
github.com/andybalholm/brotli v1.0.6 and github.com/klauspost/compress v1.17.4. Only its
u_handshake_client.go imports them: decompressCert reads a server's CompressedCertificate through
brotli.NewReader or zstd.NewReader while the client reads the server certificate, before that
certificate is verified, for an algorithm the ClientHello advertised. brotli v1.0.6 has GO-2026-6888
(excessive memory allocation on a crafted stream, fixed in v1.2.7) and compress v1.17.4 has
GO-2026-6865 (a panic on two-block frames in fse and huff0, fixed in v1.20.2). This patch moves both
requirements to those fixed releases. go mod tidy drops the go.sum lines of the old versions and adds
those of github.com/xyproto/randomstring v1.0.5, which brotli v1.2.7's go.mod requires. No Go source
changes. Upstream v26.11.9 (676eaf66f8f0) requires no brotli and klauspost/compress v1.20.1, so no
upstream commit carries this. The patch applies last, in the Dockerfile and in the make build_xray
glob alike, on the go.mod and go.sum that xray-grpc-1.83.2.patch and xray-x-net-0.60.0.patch leave.

